From 0610d4fd8f95d45c057687ed89d42098f50bb6bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 21:03:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] add marathon-mail-oauth to base image + extend
 verify-mail.sh
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Rust OAuth/Secret-Service helper packaged under
Marathon-Image/packages/marathon-mail-oauth now lands at
/usr/bin/marathon-mail-oauth via mkosi.images/base/mkosi.conf
Packages=. Marathon's mail credential plugins (marathonoauth +
marathonclassic) refuse to function without it; this is the
runtime piece that completes the Day-10 to Day-13 series.

Three new pieces in marathon-extras/:

- build-marathon-mail-oauth-apk.sh: podman+abuild wrapper that
  mirrors build-marathon-shell-apk.sh's shape. Tar-streams the
  Marathon-Shell tree into the abuild distfiles cache so cargo
  builds against the local tree when MARATHON_SHELL_SRC is set.
  Uses --net=host because abuild's options="net" allow-list still
  hits crates.io's CDN through host networking.

- build-marathon-shell-apk.sh: added qmf-dev install from
  /local-apks (mounted RO from mkosi.packages/). Without this the
  marathon-shell cmake configure step couldn't find libQmfClient
  and MARATHON_HAS_QMF stayed FALSE, silently dropping the entire
  Mail backend from the resulting apk.

- verify-mail.sh: hard-asserts /usr/bin/marathon-mail-oauth exists
  and is +x, then runs a smoke command with the permission gate
  cleared. Confirms the binary loads under musl AND that the
  env-var gate from Day 10 refuses Secret-Service access with the
  structured "permission_denied" JSON envelope. Together with the
  earlier 2b checks (libmarathonoauth.so, libmarathonclassic.so,
  MarathonOS.Services qmldir) the harness now covers every Mail
  artefact end-to-end — 12/12 green on r66 + marathon-mail-oauth.
